From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Fri, 09 Oct 2026 10:06:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: follow the driver rewrite of a background chain request

mt7996 with an iFEM front end runs a 160 MHz background chain request
as one 80 MHz half and reports that half in its CAC events. hostapd
matches a chain event by the frequency of its record. The CAC-STARTED
event of the half therefore sets the flag of a main CAC, and the
CAC-COMPLETED event never matches the chain. A radar on the operating
channel then finds the chain still in its CAC, and the AP stays.

hostapd now rewrites the whole record to the half when a CAC-STARTED
event reports it. The later events of the half match the chain, and a
radar on the operating channel moves the AP onto the half at 80 MHz.
Only the STARTED event rewrites the record, because the kernel passes
on the CAC-COMPLETED event of another radio without its source. An
event on the AP channel keeps the record, because that CAC is the CAC
of the AP.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 src/ap/dfs.c |   37 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 37 insertions(+)

--- a/src/ap/dfs.c
+++ b/src/ap/dfs.c
@@ -1904,6 +1904,42 @@ int hostapd_is_dfs_required(struct hosta
 }
 
 
+/*
+ * mt7996 with an iFEM runs a 160 MHz background request as one 80 MHz half
+ * and reports the CAC of that half. Only the STARTED event follows the
+ * request; a COMPLETED event can come from another radio. A CAC on the
+ * AP channel is the CAC of the AP, also inside the block of the chain.
+ */
+static void dfs_chain_half_adopt(struct hostapd_iface *iface, int freq,
+				 int chan_width, int cf1)
+{
+	int center = 5000 + iface->radar_background.centr_freq_seg0_idx * 5;
+	u8 chan;
+
+	if (!dfs_use_radar_background(iface) ||
+	    iface->radar_background.channel == -1 ||
+	    !iface->radar_background.cac_started || freq == iface->freq ||
+	    iface->radar_background.chwidth != CONF_OPER_CHWIDTH_160MHZ ||
+	    chan_width != CHAN_WIDTH_80 || abs(cf1 - center) != 40 ||
+	    abs(freq - cf1) >= 40 ||
+	    ieee80211_freq_to_chan(freq, &chan) == NUM_HOSTAPD_MODES)
+		return;
+
+	wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG,
+		   "DFS: background chain runs the 80 MHz half at %d MHz",
+		   cf1);
+	iface->radar_background.freq = freq;
+	iface->radar_background.channel = chan;
+	/* a wide event carries no offset; calculate_chan_offset() rule */
+	iface->radar_background.secondary_channel =
+		(abs(freq - (cf1 - 30)) / 20) % 2 == 0 ? 1 : -1;
+	iface->radar_background.chwidth =
+		chan_width_to_oper_chwidth(chan_width);
+	iface->radar_background.centr_freq_seg0_idx = (cf1 - 5000) / 5;
+	iface->radar_background.centr_freq_seg1_idx = 0;
+}
+
+
 int hostapd_dfs_start_cac(struct hostapd_data *hapd, int freq,
 			  int ht_enabled, int chan_offset, int chan_width,
 			  int cf1, int cf2)
@@ -1917,6 +1953,7 @@ int hostapd_dfs_start_cac(struct hostapd
 		return 0;
 	}
 
+	dfs_chain_half_adopt(iface, freq, chan_width, cf1);
 	if (hostapd_dfs_is_background_event(iface, freq)) {
 		iface->radar_background.cac_started = 1;
 	} else {
